# SPA fallback for the production build only.
#
# This app is one dist/index.html with React Router handling routes like
# /admin or /hub client-side. That works fine when you *navigate* there
# from inside the app, but a hard refresh or typed URL sends a real
# request for e.g. /admin, which isn't a real file on the deployed static
# site and 404s without this rule.
#
# Deliberately NOT in netlify.toml's [[redirects]]: that file is read by
# both the real production deploy AND local `netlify dev`. Locally there's
# no built dist/ yet — Vite's own dev server already serves index.html for
# unmatched client routes on its own — so a toml-level catch-all had
# nothing useful to do locally, but it still intercepted Vite's internal
# dev requests (things like /@vite/client, which have no file extension
# and aren't real files either), breaking local dev entirely (Vite's
# import-analysis choked trying to parse index.html's HTML as JS).
#
# A public/_redirects file only gets copied into dist/ during
# `pnpm run build:client`, so it ships with the production deploy and is
# never present during local dev at all — no conflict possible.
/*    /index.html   200
